The dependency from "IncompleteQuestionsFirstTest" to "IncompleteQuestionsSecondTest" in the task graph is unnecessary because the completion of the first test does not affect the second test. Each test is independent and should be calculated separately based on its own parameters (number of questions, time available, and rate of completion). Therefore, the tasks related to the first test should not influence or depend on those for the second test.

To clarify, here’s a revised version of the task graph without this unnecessary dependency:

```json
{
    "owner_agent": "ProbStat",
    "tasks": {
        "CalculateTimeForFirstTest": "Determine the time Mark spent on the first test",
        "QuestionsCompletedFirstTest": "Calculate how many questions were completed in the first test",
        "IncompleteQuestionsFirstTest": "Calculate incomplete questions for the first test",
        "CalculateTimeForSecondTest": "Determine the time Mark spent on the second test",
        "QuestionsCompletedSecondTest": "Calculate how many questions were completed in the second test",
        "IncompleteQuestionsSecondTest": "Calculate incomplete questions for the second test"
    },
    "orders": [
        {
            "condition": "success",
            "from": "CalculateTimeForFirstTest",
            "to": "QuestionsCompletedFirstTest"
        },
        {
            "condition": "success",
            "from": "QuestionsCompletedFirstTest",
            "to": "IncompleteQuestionsFirstTest"
        },
        {
            "condition": "success",
            "from": "CalculateTimeForSecondTest",
            "to": "QuestionsCompletedSecondTest"
        },
        {
            "condition": "success",
            "from": "QuestionsCompletedSecondTest",
            "to": "IncompleteQuestionsSecondTest"
        }
    ],
    "refused": false,
    "answer": null
}
```

This revised structure ensures that each test is handled independently, making the task graph more accurate and efficient.
